'''
{'cve_id': 'CVE-2016-9389', 'vulnerability_behavior': {'preconditions_for_vulnerability': 'Lack of domain consistency check before applying color transforms.', 'trigger_condition': 'An attacker provides an image with components having different domains, leading to incorrect operations in the RCT or ICT functions.', 'specific_code_behavior_causing_vulnerability': 'The code applies RCT or ICT transformations without verifying that all components have the same domain. This can result in assertion failures or incorrect image processing.'}, 'solution_behavior': 'To mitigate the vulnerability, it is necessary to add checks to ensure that all components of the image have the same domain before applying the RCT or ICT transformations. If the domains do not match, the function should return an error to prevent assertion failures and other related issues. In this case, the solution involves adding calls to jas_image_cmpt_domains_same before performing the RCT or ICT transformations.'}
